{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1329","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1329","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1329\",\"parent_revision\":\"f8f17d36d28fbc1ea6ceff94439d0e64dc8eadea81da48e72b86d944304f020a\",\"root_revision\":\"f8f17d36d28fbc1ea6ceff94439d0e64dc8eadea81da48e72b86d944304f020a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe migration process guards added in commit f230ae0d use keyword-heuristic detection (scanning issue titles, bodies, and acceptance_criteria text) to identify migration tasks. This is fragile \u2014 keyword misses are silent failures.\\n\\nReplace with schema-enforced detection by adding a `task_type` field to the Task model:\\n\\n```python\\nclass TaskType(str, Enum):\\n    migration = \\\"migration\\\"\\n    feature = \\\"feature\\\"\\n    refactor = \\\"refactor\\\"\\n    bugfix = \\\"bugfix\\\"\\n    chore = \\\"chore\\\"\\n\\n# In Task model:\\ntask_type: TaskType | None = None\\n```\\n\\nWhen `task_type == \\\"migration\\\"` is set, complete-implementation Pre-Phase 1a activates unconditionally rather than relying on keyword scan.\\n\\nAuthoritative model: plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py\\nGuards that would use this field: complete-implementation Pre-Phase 1a, rt-ica Data Deletion Fidelity trigger, planner-rt-ica hard-block rule.\\n\\nNot blocking current guards \u2014 keyword detection is functional. This is a quality improvement to make detection reliable and explicit.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `sam_schema/core/models.py` Task model location | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n| 2 | Guards that would use `task_type` | AVAILABLE | Item description: complete-implementation, rt-ica, planner-rt-ica |\\n| 3 | Backward compat with existing task files | AVAILABLE | Optional field with None default |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 fully specified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature (typing improvement). Low complexity. Additive field; backward compatible. Strengthens type safety.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `TaskType(str, Enum)` defined with values: `migration`, `feature`, `refactor`, `bugfix`, `chore`\\n- `Task.task_type: TaskType | None = None` field added to the Task model in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py`\\n- When `task_type == 'migration'`, `complete-implementation` Pre-Phase 1a activates unconditionally (no keyword scan needed)\\n- Existing keyword-scan guards remain functional as fallback when `task_type` is None\\n- `ty check` passes; no `dict[str, Any]` or bare `str` for this field\\n- Existing task files without `task_type` field load correctly (field is Optional with None default)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 add TaskType enum and Task.task_type field\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/` \u2014 update Pre-Phase 1a to check task_type\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document task_type field\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a SAM task author and migration-guard implementer, I need a `task_type` enum field on the Task model so migration task detection is schema-enforced rather than fragile keyword heuristics that can silently miss tasks.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add task-type field to sam_schema/core/models.py for schema-enforced migration detection** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: P964 RCA \u2014 plan hidden-sprouting-pebble follow-up items\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0145d8832e0a3319c7bda5957f49ae68b9a7930ed9eb1774c6d224a2955554fc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS9UXg\"}"}